WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.135
Your team rents a giant AI model by the token

2
00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:05.710
to do the same small job, over and over.

3
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.670
Your CFO wants the bill down.

4
00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.400
Your engineers want proof it won't break.

5
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.882
FallForge Mint starts with one question:

6
00:00:12.882 --> 00:00:14.192
which model is enough?

7
00:00:14.192 --> 00:00:18.777
The sizer suggests the smallest open-weight model that should clear your bar.

8
00:00:18.777 --> 00:00:21.140
A one-billion answer says one billion.

9
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.679
Mint it from a few of your own examples.

10
00:00:23.679 --> 00:00:27.887
Then it tries to beat the base model on examples kept out of its spec

11
00:00:27.887 --> 00:00:29.450
and it can say you lost.

12
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.150
You get a signed scorecard.

13
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.646
The held-out answers weren't in the spec we gave the model.

14
00:00:34.646 --> 00:00:35.990
Anyone can re-run it.

15
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.047
At high use, owning can run six to seventeen times cheaper.

16
00:00:40.047 --> 00:00:42.830
When renting wins, it says keep renting.

17
00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:43.711
One file.

18
00:00:43.711 --> 00:00:44.839
Your machine.

19
00:00:44.839 --> 00:00:45.720
No meter.

20
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.322
And Forge is one door into a whole sovereign estate.

21
00:00:49.322 --> 00:00:51.240
Seven stages, one pipeline.

22
00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.370
Gated builds ride a trust rail:

23
00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.792
it breaks the code to test the tests.

24
00:00:55.792 --> 00:00:59.690
It even found a line left-pad's passing tests don't check.

25
00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.674
In fall-os, you hatch your own assistant and level it into your own

26
00:01:03.674 --> 00:01:04.760
operating system.

27
00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.827
The dispatcher routes every job:

28
00:01:06.827 --> 00:01:11.068
seven organs run themselves, nine wait for a human key, and eight are

29
00:01:11.068 --> 00:01:12.520
honestly marked to-do.

30
00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.434
Peers connect directly, no server between

31
00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:18.210
and sovereign-foundry ties it together.

32
00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.403
Models trained on their own output lose the tails.

33
00:01:21.403 --> 00:01:24.002
A mesh of real people is the clean signal.

34
00:01:24.002 --> 00:01:26.020
Owned, provable AI is the moat.

35
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.909
AI Native Solutions.

36
00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:28.535
Own it.

37
00:01:28.535 --> 00:01:29.690
Prove it.

